# Celestial Reunion's behold of two creatures of a type is any mix of creatures you control and creature cards in your hand
# (a ruling). Bot1 beholds the Elvish Mystic on its battlefield and the one in its hand (only the card in the hand is
# revealed). The type question offers only the types two beholdable creatures share: with one Birds of Paradise, Bird is not
# offered (the refusal), and a Bird and a Mystic are not two of a type (the refused pair). The Mystic found is an Elf, so it enters the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Celestial Reunion
Elvish Mystic
Elvish Mystic
Birds of Paradise
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Celestial Reunion.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Modes(Choose a creature type and behold two creatures of that type)
! Bot1.Modes(Bird)
Bot1.Modes(Elf)
! Bot1.Choose(Bot1.Hand.Birds of Paradise)
Bot1.Choose(Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic; Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic)
? Bot1.Revealed = Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Search(Elvish Mystic)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot1.Hand = Elvish Mystic; Birds of Paradise
Bot1.Graveyard = Celestial Reunion
